### What is the REST API for managing connectors?

In distributed mode, every worker exposes a REST API on port 8083. Changes propagate across the cluster through the internal config topic, so you can call any worker. The key endpoints handle the full lifecycle of connectors.

At National Bank of India, Rajesh manages the transaction ingestion pipeline entirely through these API calls.

```bash
# List all running connectors
curl http://localhost:8083/connectors

# Create a new connector
curl -X POST http://localhost:8083/connectors \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "bank-txn-source",
    "config": {
      "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSourceConnector",
      "tasks.max": "3",
      "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://bankdb:5432/nbi",
      "table.whitelist": "transactions",
      "mode": "incrementing",
      "incrementing.column.name": "txn_id",
      "topic.prefix": "bank."
    }
  }'

# Check status of a connector and its tasks
curl http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source/status

# Pause a connector (stops all its tasks)
curl -X PUT http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source/pause

# Resume a paused connector
curl -X PUT http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source/resume

# Restart a failed task (task 0)
curl -X POST http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source/tasks/0/restart

# Update connector configuration
curl -X PUT http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source/config \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSourceConnector",
    "tasks.max": "5",
    "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://bankdb:5432/nbi",
    "table.whitelist": "transactions,accounts",
    "mode": "incrementing",
    "incrementing.column.name": "txn_id",
    "topic.prefix": "bank."
  }'

# Delete a connector
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8083/connectors/bank-txn-source
```

